        "full_content": "How to watch Arsenal vs Coventry: Live streams, team news and TV channels for the Premier League 2026/27 game\nAway at the champions is as tough as it gets for Coventry on their EPL return\n- Watch Arsenal vs Coventry on USA Network via Sling (US)\n- Unlock your stream with NordVPN (save 75%)\n- Arsenal vs Coventry kick-off: Fri, Aug 21 at 3pm ET / 8pm BST\nToday's Arsenal vs Coventry live stream serves up a momentous fixture a quarter of a century in the making. Taking place 25 years and 94 days since the Sky Blues were relegated from the top flight in 2001 – the longest such gap in Premier League history – it's an occasion to savour, even though the schedulers have been far from kind.\nArsenal at the Emirates stands to be the toughest test Coventry will face all season. Mikel Arteta's side had a formidable home record last term, with 16 wins, two defeats and a draw, and the relief of finally fulfilling their Premier League title ambitions combined with the summer signings of Christos Tzolis and Bruno Guimaraes, have had a transformative effect.\nThe Gunners' performance in the Community Shield last weekend suggested that they've added silk to their steel. Man City were their closest challengers for the title last season, and although they're now in the early stages of a new regime, blowing them away in the manner Arsenal did was quite a statement. While Tzolis was their standout performer, Bruno not only slotted in seamlessly for Declan Rice, but brought the best out of Martin Odegaard too. The Brazilian, however, is sidelined tonight.\nFor fans of a certain vintage, Coventry's return to the big time brings back sun-kissed memories of cult heroes like Mustapha Hadji and Youssef Chippo, and new signings Gustavo Hamer and Taiwo Awoniyi certainly have the mercurial talent to follow in those footsteps. This early on, however, Frank Lampard has opted for a safety-first approach.\nHere's how to watch Arsenal vs Coventry in the 2026/27 Premier Le