        "full_content": "Samsung Galaxy S25 Ultra price drop alert! Get flagship device with a discount of over Rs 30000 on Amazon\nSamsung Galaxy S25 Ultra gets a major price cut on Amazon.\nBuyers can save more through bank and exchange offers.\nThe flagship offers powerful performance, premium design and advanced cameras.\nIf you’ve been eyeing to grab a flagship device, then the last-generation flagship device, the Samsung Galaxy S25, is currently selling with a heavy discount on Amazon. Aside from the flat price reduction, the consumers can also club in bank and card offers to further reduce the net effective price of the smartphone. The handset comes packed with the Snapdragon 8 Elite chipset and offers up to 12GB of RAM and 1TB of internal storage. Not only that, but at the rear end you also get a quad-camera setup to ensure that you can capture all the important moments in the highest quality. However, one thing to keep in mind is that it’s a limited-time offer and may end soon. Here is a clear breakdown of how the Samsung Galaxy S25 Ultra deal works on Amazon.\nSamsung Galaxy S25 Ultra Amazon deal\nThe Samsung Galaxy S25 Ultra debuted in the Indian market with a price tag of Rs 129,999, but Amazon has currently listed it for just Rs 94,999, which is a flat discount of Rs 35,000. Consumers using the Amazon ICICI Bank credit card to make the purchase can save an extra 5 per cent if they are prime members. However, the non-prime members can also get a decent 3 per cent extra discount.\nFor the users who don’t want to pay the whole price upfront, the e-commerce brand is also offering no-cost EMI starting at just Rs 3,340 per month. You can also check out the exchange programme on Amazon if you’re upgrading. Depending on the brand model and working condition of your old model, you can get an exchange bonus of up to Rs 33,500. Do note that these offers are available for a limited period and may change depending on stock availability.\nSamsung Galaxy S25 Ultra: Is it the right time to buy?\nThe smartphone prices are going up due to the ongoing global scarcity of the memory chipset. The Samsung S25 series has also faced the heat, as certain variants of the Samsung Galaxy S25 model recently received a price hike.\nConsidering these situations, the current price drop on the Galaxy S25 Ultra indeed makes it a steal deal. The smartphone offers you a 6.9-inch QHD+ Dynamic AMOLED 2X display coupled with an adaptive refresh rate that goes up to 120Hz.\nUnder the hood, the smartphone runs on the Snapdragon 8 Elite chipset paired with up to 12GB of RAM and 1TB of storage, ensuring that you receive a smooth performance when gaming or multitasking. Moreover, it also provides you with the AI-enabled functionalities.\nAlso read: Want to buy iPhone 16? You can save over Rs 9,000 on Flipkart, here is how\nTalking about the camera, the Galaxy S25 Ultra features a 200MP primary camera, a 50MP ultrawide lens, a 50MP telephoto sensor with 5x optical zoom, and a 10MP 3x telephoto camera. For selfies and video calls, the device houses a 12MP front-facing camera.\nTo ensure that you can perform your daily tasks without any interruptions, the device also comes packed with a 5,000mAh battery. If you’re someone who prefers premium build quality, good cameras, and long-term software updates, then this smartphone is just for you.\nBhaskar is a Senior Copy Editor at Digit India who keeps a close watch on everything shaping the world of technology from smartphones and home appliances to AI, government tech initiatives, digital safety, and the latest industry developments. Whether it's breaking news, in-depth features, hands-on reviews, practical how-to guides, or exclusive scoops, he translates complex tech into stories that are easy to understand and worth reading. His work has been featured in iGeeksBlog, GuidingTech, and other leading publications. Before joining Digit India, he served as an assistant editor at TechBloat. A B.Tech graduate and full-ti