        "full_content": "Vivo T5 5G to launch soon with a big battery: Check expected specs, price and more\nVivo T5 5G is expected to launch soon in India.\nThe phone may feature a Snapdragon 7s Gen 4 chip and 7,500mAh battery.\nIt could offer a 120Hz AMOLED display and a multi-camera setup.\nVivo is all set to expand its mid-range smartphone segment with the upcoming Vivo T5 5G. The smartphone will be joining the Vivo T5 series that currently has the Vivo T5 Lite and Vivo T5 Pro. While the company has been tight-lipped about the upcoming device, the leaks and rumours have painted a clear picture of what to expect from the device. The smartphone is said to run on Qualcomm’s Snapdragon 7s Gen 4 processor and house a 7,500mAh battery. Moreover, it’s also tipped to get a dual-camera setup at the back. Here’s everything from the launch timeline, expected price and specs we know about the Vivo T5 5G.\nVivo T5: Launch timeline (Teased)\nVivo has recently put up the micro-site for the T5 5G model on Flipkart, confirming that the launch of the device is not so far away. However, the company refrained from announcing the exact launch date of the smartphone.\nVivo T5: Price (Expected)\nEarly reports suggest that the smartphone can land in the Indian markets with a price somewhere between Rs 34,999 and Rs 49,999. However, keep in mind that these are just speculations, and the official price will only be revealed at the time of launch and may be different.\nVivo T5: Specs (Expected)\nThe Vivo T5 5G is expected to feature a 6.7-inch AMOLED display with a 120Hz refresh rate and curved edges. Under the hood, it’s anticipated to draw its power from Qualcomm’s Snapdragon 7s Gen 4 processor, which may get paired with 8GB of RAM and up to 128GB of internal storage options.\nOut of the box the device is expected to run on OriginOS 6, a skin based on Android 16. Moreover, the device may also bring certain AI features. The handset is tipped to pack a 7,500mAh battery with support for 100W fast charging.\nTo please the camera enthusiasts, the T5 5G may feature a triple rear camera setup, including a 50MP main camera with optical image stabilisation, a 13MP ultrawide lens and an 8MP periscope telephoto sensor. At the front the device may boast a 32MP sensor for selfies and video calls.\nBhaskar is a Senior Copy Editor at Digit India who keeps a close watch on everything shaping the world of technology from smartphones and home appliances to AI, government tech initiatives, digital safety, and the latest industry developments. Whether it's breaking news, in-depth features, hands-on reviews, practical how-to guides, or exclusive scoops, he translates complex tech into stories that are easy to understand and worth reading. His work has been featured in iGeeksBlog, GuidingTech, and other leading publications. Before joining Digit India, he served as an assistant editor at TechBloat. A B.Tech graduate and full-time tech journalist, he is driven by just one goal, which is to help readers stay informed, stay secure, and stay ahead in an ever-changing digital world. View Full Profile",
