\nBuild and manage a successful user experience team\nOrchestrate and optimize research to amplify its impact\nStudy your users’ real-life behaviors and make data-informed design decisions\nKeep pace with a rapidly evolving field\nWrite clear, effective UX copy and learn how to use AI tools responsibly and strategically\nStrategically combine content, visuals, and interactive components to design successful web pages\nLead goal-based group activities to make decisions and establish alignment\nApply practical leadership skills to your UX role, regardless of your title\nConduct successful discovery phases to ensure you build the best solution\nTurn AI ideas into evidence-backed strategic direction through evaluation, prioritization, and cross-functional facilitation\nCreate a seamless, cohesive cross-channel experience\nUse psychology to predict and explain how your customers think and act\nTechniques and tools for implementing an actionable content strategy\nDefine, share, and implement design operations\nApply systematic analyses to uncover themes and user insights\nCalculate, interpret, and report the numbers from your quantitative UX studies\nDesign innovative, trusted, and useful AI products and features\nOrganize and structure information to improve findability and discoverability\nPersuade and engage while presenting research findings and design ideas\nUnderstand UX and product roles (PM and PO) to better collaborate in product development\nCapture and communicate UX insights across complex interactions\nGet Help Choosing Courses:\nSelect the category which describes you, and scroll up for highlighted course suggestions.\nNN/g UX Certification is an exam-based credential which reinforces learning and increases your credibility. Earn a UX Certificate by attending any 5 courses, and passing the related exams.\n| Pay by the Course | Until September 11 | Until October 2 | Until October 16 | \n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 Course | $1210 | $1260 | $1310 | \n| 2 Courses 10% off each | $2178 | $2268 | $2358 | \n| 3 Courses 15% off each | $3086 | $3213 | $3341 | \n| 4 Courses 18% off each | $3969 | $4133 | $4297 | \n| 5 Courses 20% off each | $4840 | $5040 | $5240 | \nPrices shown here are in U.S. Dollars (USD). Discounts are based on the number of courses purchased during the same event. If you choose to change your course enrollment after purchase, you may forfeit the discount and need to pay additional fees.\nMeetings will take place using the video conferencing tool Zoom, collaboration tools (such as group document editing and whiteboarding tools), and the social discussion tool Slack.\nYou'll also be able to use Slack before, during, and after the event to participate in social events and network with other participants.\nTo participate in interactive live courses and exercises with other course participants, you will need:\nHere are the start and end times for courses at this event. Each course meets in 2 sessions, over 2 consecutive days. You must attend both days in order to be eligible to take the UX Certification exam.\n| Time Zone | Course Session Starts | Course Session Ends | \n|---|---|---|\n| San Francisco | 8 AM | 11:30 AM | \n| New York City | 11 AM | 2:30 PM | \n| London | 4 PM | 7:30 PM | \n| Amsterdam/Berlin | 5 PM | 8:30 PM | \nNo. These are live events that rely heavily on audience interaction and small-group activities in online breakout rooms. Thus, a recording would not have the same instructional value, thus we will not offer this.\nYes. This not only speeds registration but also ensures you'll get a seat in the sessions you want.\nYes. Attend at least 5 courses and pass all 5 exams to earn an NN/G UX Certificate. You can take the 5 courses all at this event, or take some at this event and the rest at a future event.\nYou must sign in at the start of class, and attend the full day. At the end of the course each day, the online exam will be available for that day's classes. You will be able to log in, pay exam fees (if they were not already paid when you registered), and take the exam. You can take your exams the same day, or any time within 35 calendar days after the conference.\nYou may pay your tuition and exam fees by credit card, or bank transfer.\n            The following credit cards are accepted:\n            \n              \nIf you must cancel after registering, your registration fee will be refunded less a 20% handling fee, provided that written notice of cancellation is received by September 25, 2026. After that, no refunds will be granted, but we will accept a substitute attendee if we receive a written note from the registered attendee stating his or her intention to transfer registration to a named individual. Email events@nngroup.com with cancellation, substitution, or refund requests.\nAbsolutely. Our website uses Secure Sockets Layer (SSL) technology to encrypt your personal information when you place your order. This means that your order cannot be read as it travels over the Internet, so your name, address, and credit card information are secure.\nIf you receive an error message when you try to register, restarting your browser may resolve the issue. You can also contact us at events@nngroup.com or +1(415) 685-4230 and we will be happy to assist you.\nThe Terms and Conditions for the UX Conference and UX Certification Program provide more detailed information about policies, privacy, and the Code of Conduct for training participants.\nPlease contact us at events@nngroup.com or +1(415) 685-4230",
