        "link": "https://pib.gov.in/PressReleaseIframePage.aspx?PRID=2302084",
        "source": "Press Information Bureau",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-21T20:40:18.248781+00:00",
        "image": "https:/pib.gov.in/images/indian-emblem.png",
        "full_content": "                        \n                              National Financial Reporting Authority\n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                              \n                              \n                                    National Financial Reporting Authority (NFRA) conducts sixth outreach programmes with focus on small and medium auditors under the theme “Creating a Better Financial Reporting Ecosystem” in Ahmedabad\n                              \n                              \n                                    \nThe outreach aims to support professional capacity, strengthen audit quality and improve the quality of financial reporting \n                              \n                        \n                        \n                              प्रविष्टि तिथि:\n                21 AUG 2026 6:45PM by PIB Delhi\n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        The National Financial Reporting Authority (NFRA) completed its sixth outreach programme at Ahmedabad recently, in a series of outreach programmes that commenced in 2025. The  programme with the theme “Creating a Better Financial Reporting Ecosystem”, was inaugurated by Nitin Gupta, Chairperson, NFRA and CA Prasanna Kumar D, President, of ICAI.\nWith the focus on small and medium auditors and an aim to support in professional capacity, strengthen audit quality and improve the quality of financial reporting, this was the second such outreach programme held in collaboration with the Institute of Chartered Accountants of India (ICAI), the first being at Pune in June 2026. \nShri Nitin Gupta, Chairperson, NFRA, in his keynote address, emphasised the pivotal role of the accountancy profession in safeguarding public interest and building trust in financial reporting. Shri Gupta emphasised the need to remain aligned with contemporary global standards and called upon the audit firms to continuously enhance their competencies, including adopting appropriate technology in the audit process. \nIn his address, CA Prasanna Kumar D, President ICAI, stated that audit quality in financial reporting is critical for building trust and confidence among the stakeholders. \nMs Smita Jhingran, Full-Time Member, NFRA, highlighted the importance of NFRA's inspection of audit firms in ensuring high-quality financial reporting.\nThe experts’ sessions aimed at providing practical insights for improving audit quality in day-to-day professional work and comprised technical sessions on key aspects such as Audit Strategy Documentation, Risk of Material Mis-statements, and case studies on takeaways from NFRA's oversight.\nSince this initiative was launched last year, NFRA’s outreach programmes have elicited participation from representatives of more than 450 small and medium firms.\n \n                        *****\nSR/ONP\n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        (रिलीज़ आईडी: 2302084)\n                        \tआगंतुक पटल  : 174\n                        \n                              \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                              \n                        \n                        \n                              \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                        \n                              \n                        \n                   \n                  ",
