        "full_content": "As the new Telegraph Fantasy Football season approaches, the fantasy football experts at Fantasy Football Hub will continue to bring you the very best in fantasy football knowledge, tips and tools to help you rise up the ranks and win your mini-leagues.\nTo join the Hub and get access to all their great resources and expert tips you can take advantage of its 50% pre-season discount here.\n  \nPicking your team: getting the right balance\nOne of the trickiest parts of selecting your Telegraph Fantasy Football team is deciding how to distribute your transfer budget.\nShould you go big on an expensive strikeforce? Is devoting mega bucks to your backline in a quest for clean sheets the way to go? Are there any budget gems out there primed to take the Premier League by storm?\nTo help you decide on your transfer strategy, we have put together a team-by-team guide with three selections from each team for you to consider from the big hitting favourites, to the underpriced minnows.\n \nArsenal\n- 1st: Magalhães (£4.9m)\n- 2nd: Mosquera (£3.7m)\n- 3rd: Tzolis (£4.0m)\nAston Villa\n- 1st: Gomes (£3.3m)\n- 2nd: Buendia (£3.6m)\n- 3rd: Konsa (£3.5m)\nBournemouth\n- 1st: Scott (£2.8m)\n- 2nd: Hill (£2.6m)\n- 3rd: Rayan (£3.6m)\nBrentford\n- 1st: Thiago (£4.6m)\n- 2nd: Sangaré (£3.1m)\n- 3rd: Schade (£3.6m)\nBrighton and Hove Albion\n- 1st: Vušković (£2.8m)\n- 2nd: Hinshelwood (£2.8m)\n- 3rd: Groß (£3.7m)\n \nChelsea\n- 1st: Pedro (£5.1m)\n- 2nd: Palestra (£2.7m)\n- 3rd: Rogers (£4.3m)\nCoventry City\n- 1st: Grimes (£2.5m)\n- 2nd: Rushworth (£2.6m)\n- 3rd: Thomas (£2.3m)\nCrystal Palace\n- 1st: Sarr (£3.9m)\n- 2nd: Canvot (£2.5m)\n- 3rd: Mitchell (£3.6m)\nEverton\n- 1st: Ndiaye (£3.3m)\n- 2nd: Garner (£3.1m)\n- 3rd: Dewsbury-Hall (£3.7m)\nFulham\n- 1st: Garcia (£3.7m)\n- 2nd: Palacios (£2.8m)\n- 3rd: Charles (£2.9m)\nHull City\n- 1st: McBurnie (£2.9m)\n- 2nd: Slater (£2.5m)\n- 3rd: Giles (£2.6m)\nIpswich Town\n- 1st: Davis (£2.6m)\n- 2nd: Maeda (£2.8m)\n-