        "image": "https://wpblogassets.paytm.com/paytmblog/uploads/2021/11/2_Metro_Paytm-Karo-to-get-Delhi-metro-tickets.jpg",
        "full_content": "Travelling by Delhi Metro is the fastest way across the city, and buying the ticket no longer means standing in line. You can purchase a Delhi Metro QR ticket in the Paytm app and walk straight to the gate.\nThis article covers the step by step purchase process, current fares, the validity and penalty rules that apply to QR tickets, and practical tips for a smooth journey.\nHow to Purchase Delhi Metro QR Tickets Using Paytm\nBuying your ticket takes under a minute. You choose your origin and destination, set the number of passengers, and pay.\nStep 1: Open the Paytm app on your smartphone.\nStep 2: On the home screen, find the “Recharge & Bill Payments” section.\nStep 3: Tap “View More” to see additional options.\nStep 4: Select the “Metro” icon from the expanded list.\nStep 5: Choose the “Metro QR Ticket” option.\nStep 6: Select your From Station and To Station.\nStep 7: Enter the number of passengers. You can book for up to 6 passengers in a single transaction.\nStep 8: Review the fare and tap “Proceed to Pay.”\nStep 9: Complete the payment using UPI, debit card, credit card\nStep 10: Your QR ticket is generated in the app immediately. Scan it at the entry gate of your origin station and again at the exit gate of your destination.\nNote that entry is permitted only from the station you selected while booking. If you enter from a different station, the QR code will not open the gate and the ticket is not refunded.\nDelhi Metro Fares 2026\nFares on the main Delhi Metro network follow six distance slabs. These rates took effect on 25 August 2025, the first revision in eight years.\nThe Airport Express Line, also called the Orange Line, has a separate fare table ranging from ₹11 to ₹75. New Delhi to IGI Airport Terminal 3 costs ₹64, New Delhi to Shivaji Stadium costs ₹21, New Delhi to Dhaula Kuan costs ₹43, and the extended stretch to Yashobhoomi Dwarka Sector 25 is the highest at ₹75.\nA few points on pricing worth knowing. QR tickets are charged at the standard fare with no discount. A DMRC smart card gives 10% off every journey plus a further discount during off-peak hours, so frequent commuters still save more with a card. DMRC does not offer concessional fares for students, senior citizens or other categories on single journey tickets.\nQR Ticket Validity and Penalty Rules\nThese rules apply to Delhi Metro QR tickets regardless of which app you use to purchase them. Knowing them can help you avoid penalties during your journey.\n- Same-day validity: The ticket is valid only on the calendar day of purchase, until 11:30 PM. It cannot be carried over to the next day.\n- Origin station locked: You can enter the metro only from the station selected while booking the ticket.\n- One QR code per passenger: If you book tickets for multiple passengers, each passenger receives a separate QR code. Each QR code must be scanned separately.\n- Maximum travel time: Exceeding the permitted journey time may attract a penalty of ₹10 per hour, capped at ₹50 on the main network. On the Airport Express Line, the maximum permitted journey time is 65 minutes, with a penalty of ₹20 per hour, capped at ₹400.\n- Same-station exit: If you enter and exit from the same station, you must do so within 20 minutes. Beyond this period, the applicable ₹10 per hour penalty may be charged.\n- No valid ticket at the exit: If you cannot produce a valid QR ticket at the exit gate, you may be treated as travelling without a ticket and charged the maximum fare for the network plus a ₹50 penalty.\nBenefits of Using Paytm for Delhi Metro QR Tickets\n- Save time: Skip token counters and vending machine queues, which can be especially busy between 8:30 AM and 10:30 AM and 5:30 PM and 8:30 PM.\n- Buy from anywhere: Purchase your ticket from home, while travelling in a cab, or outside the station, as long as you have an internet connection.\n- Instant ticket generation: Your QR code is generated as soon as the payment is successful.\n- Group booking: Book tickets for up to 6 passengers in a single transaction instead of buying individual tokens.\n- Digital record: Your tickets and payment details remain available in your app history, making it easier to track commute expenses or claim reimbursements.\n- Contactless travel: There is no physical token to collect, carry or return.\nImportant Tips for a Smooth Metro QR Ticket Experience\n- Check the stations carefully: Confirm the From and To stations before making the payment. Entry from a different station may be refused, and the fare may not be refunded.\n- Buy within metro operating hours: Metro services on most lines generally run from around 5:00 AM to 11:00 PM. A ticket purchased after service hours cannot be used the next day.\n- Keep enough battery: You need your phone at both the entry and exit gates. If your phone runs out of battery at the exit, you may have to pay the maximum fare plus a ₹50 penalty. Charge your phone before a long journey.\n- Do not rely on a screenshot: A screenshot or photo of a QR ticket may not be accepted. Open the original ticket in the app when scanning at the gates.\n- Keep connectivity: Make sure mobile data is available so you can access your ticket at both the entry and exit gates.\n- Find the QR-enabled gates: Not every fare gate may support QR ticket scanning. Look for gates marked for QR tickets, usually one or two gates in each bank of gates at a station.\n- Secure the app: Protect your Paytm account with a PIN, pattern or biometric lock. Never share your login credentials or OTP with anyone.\n- Compare with a smart card: If you travel more than 15 to 20 times a month, a smart card with a 10% discount per ride may work out cheaper than purchasing QR tickets for every journey.",
        "content": "Travelling by Delhi Metro is the fastest way across the city, and buying the ticket no longer means standing in line. You can purchase a Delhi Metro QR ticket in the Paytm app and walk straight to the gate.\nThis article covers the step by step purchase process, current fares, the validity and penalty rules that apply to QR tickets, and practical tips for a smooth journey.\nHow to Purchase Delhi Met...",
