        "image": "https://cdn.sanity.io/images/hlcyrtq5/production/12f460da9f13988876e8d215de2ca49eff6c7516-1920x1080.webp",
        "full_content": "Transform your product operating model for the AI era\nFrom customer signals to portfolio bets, see the truth in real time. Capture work, expose drift and risk, and tie progress to revenue and outcomes.\nTrusted by\nBuild better products, ship faster\nDisconnected data and inconsistent execution lead to missed targets. Use AI-powered workflows to end the guesswork and guide everything from product discovery to launch.\nWork smarter with AI\nGet complete, real-time visibility\nAdapt to your workflow\nOne flexible system of work for strategy, delivery, and iteration\nUnify customer signals, product planning, and execution in one AI workspace. Context flows automatically, data-driven decisions speed up, and value compounds every quarter.\nAlign features to real customer needs\nManage customer feedback\nConnect all your channels in one place, and automatically identify high value opportunities.\nExtract insights automatically\nUse AI to pull key themes from feature requests, Gong calls,customer surveys, and prototype reviews, then auto-add to backlog.\nClose the loop\nCreate release notes with AI to notify users when you address feedback and release new product features.\nDrive product decisions\nAlign your product vision to company strategy\nCreate strategies and roadmaps based on your company prioritization frameworks, user feedback, and product analytics.\nOptimize team resources\nPlan for high-impact initiatives and balance capacity across product teams with AI resourcing recommendations.\nDeliver executive visibility\nTrack progress against key metrics with executive dashboards, Kanban boards, and Gantt charts– with real-time visualization.\nMaximize every sprint\nManage dependencies\nMonitor cross-functional capacity across programs.\nKeep software development in sync\nAlign planning and engineering capacity by integrating with SaaS tools like Atlassian Jira and Azure DevOps.\nDetect strategic drift\nUse AI-driven roadmapping tools to spot misalignment and course-correct quickly.\nLaunch with confidence\nAutomate launch readiness\nGenerate timelines, checklists, and release notes to ensure successful product launches.\nBoost team collaboration\nKeep marketing, sales, legal and support aligned with automated handoffs.\nTrack progress in real time\nProvide cross-functional visibility with automated status updates and dynamic roadmaps.\nUnblock everyone\nKeep teams informed\nSubscribe to sprint planning and launch timelines, and automate updates across Slack and email.\nShare customer-ready resources\nAll your assets and FAQs in one place, easily accessible for GTM teams to share out.\nSync launch details from your roadmap\nAs things change in your product development process, your timelines update automatically, keeping teams aligned.\nReal-world AI use cases with real results\nStart experimenting with workflows you can deploy right now.\nIntegrate critical workflows\nCombine all your systems into a single source of truth via integrations and APIs with Jira, Azure DevOps, and Confluence or enterprise datasets in Salesforce, Workday, and Snowflake.\nSee how real enterprise companies are using Airtable\n“We went from months of collecting and triaging and translating information into real time, literally a day, hours. Right. And all we need to do is just confirm it.”\n3x\nreduction in feedback to launch time\n“Airtable enables us to roll up hundreds of IT initiatives into a single portfolio, aligned to strategic priorities and metrics. We can adapt with the click of a button. Airtable has allowed us to be ourselves.”\n“AWS teams have used Airtable to streamline and accelerate our marketing workflows. As one of Airtable AI’s early customers, we leverage Airtable AI on Amazon Bedrock to further enhance and automate processes.”\nResources and insights to explore\nProduct roadmapping 2.0 - best practices in AI integration\nUnpack AI integration best practices for popular product roadmapping tools. Equip your business for the future with the knowledge your teams need to succeed.\nProduct roadmap examples: 8 samples to use today\nExplore 8 roadmap examples and templates to align teams, share vision, and drive strategy from idea to launch.\n25 key product management metrics & KPIs for 2026 (And how to track them)\nLearn the 25 most critical product management KPIs every PM should track, including CAC, churn rate, and NPS, plus how to calculate them and why they matter.\nFrequently asked questions\n- When evaluating product management tools, focus on features that help team members and stakeholders manage the entire product lifecycle. Look for quick-start functionality such as Microsoft Excel imports, integrations with existing product development tools, and built-in project management software. An intuitive user interface also accelerates onboarding.\n- Prioritize scalability. The best product management tools go beyond basic task management for individual products, adapting easily to new use cases as your needs evolve. And with AI assistants and tools like Airtable AI agent software and Omni, teams can analyze user behavior at scale, eliminate hours of manual work, and deliver better products with improved user experiences.\n- Don’t forget collaboration tools—both built-in and integrations with whiteboard software like Miro, communication tools like Slack, or design tools like Figma.\nJira, Align, Aha, Asana, Trello, and Productboard are the most comparable product management platforms. But only Airtable offers one connected solution across product roadmapping, feedback management, that lets product teams execute more effectively. Unlike rigid tools that force you into their framework, Airtable adapts to your unique product taxonomy—whether you organize by squads, tribes, business units, or value streams. This flexibility, combined with unified data across your entire product operation, lets teams execute more effectively while maintaining their preferred ways of working.\nYou have multiple paths to migrate your data—import spreadsheets and CSVs, connect through our extensive integration library, or use Airtable Sync to maintain live connections with your current systems. Our services team and certified partners specialize in product data migration, helping you identify which data sources matter most for your key workflows and mapping out the right approach for your organization. They'll work with you to ensure your critical product data is properly structured and flowing into Airtable, setting the foundation for your new operating model.\nAirtable works alongside Jira Software, not instead of it. While Jira excels at managing engineering sprints and tickets, product teams need a different kind of system—one that connects customer feedback to strategic planning, manages portfolio-wide roadmaps, and keeps executives aligned without forcing them into engineering workflows. Our advanced syncing means engineering keeps working in Jira while product teams get the holistic view they need to ensure every sprint advances strategic objectives. Your marketing leaders, sales teams, and executives can finally see real-time progress without navigating Jira's engineering-focused interface.\nExplore our pricing page to find flexible plans or reach out to our team to learn more.",
